ns":["Trace scope, supported predecessor coverage and acceptance mappings to the originating ISSUE reproduction, root cause and fix intent. Do not infer Epic or HLD ancestry from generated metadata.","Inspect current installer, shell, TUI, VS Code and JetBrains entry points for the proposed first-upgrade delivery matrix, pre-shutdown controller invocation, configured source preservation and older-client fallback.","Assess immutable candidate and rollback provisioning, trusted release-pair qualification, legacy commit allowlists, modified-release refusal and preservation of native dependencies and runtime.","Check stageManagedInstallation against its staging-only return contract and controller-owned activation: explicit start intent, reservation, provisional selector, job registration, idle handshake, readiness, partial-write recovery and --no-start.","Inspect running managed daemon.update integration, detached-helper acknowledgement ordering, removal of legacy shutdown scheduling, stopped local updates and unchanged IPC result shapes.","Assess errors, interruption behavior, Linux preservation, alternatives and unit/integration/macOS qualification coverage for these responsibilities. Reassess install-01 through install-04 without presuming resolution."],"dependsOn":[],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"cutover","title":"Predecessor contracts, legacy exclusion, ownership transfer and durable recovery","selectors":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/migration","/body/testStrategy","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/citations/9","/citations/10","/citations/11","/citations/12","/citations/13"],"concerns":["Inspect the proposed managed, legacy-job, legacy-direct and legacy-stopped predecessor variants, required persisted evidence, historical decoding, rejection rules and recovery dispatch against actual gate and recovery contracts.","Assess state-root, selector, supervisor, child, reservation and immutable-release ownership/cardinality. Verify direct rollback argv/cwd/environment recipes and exact recovery LaunchAgent loader arguments and restart policy.","Check feasibility and recovery of atomic canonical-checkout exchange, displaced-directory preservation, journaled inode evidence, old helper/process admission and supported-launch-route exclusion.","Inspect actual run-file guard lifetime, store-opening order and proposed controller-to-supervisor guard transfer for an enforceable exclusion boundary, including old callers that ignore the new reservation.","Trace authenticated shutdown and independent exact-incarnation exit observation through graceful, broker-denied and unknown classifications, crash-consistent release qualification, cleanup and user-visible results.","Distinguish provisional selector publication from terminal outcome publication. Verify durable-success recovery, uncertain acknowledgements, candidate cleanup, predecessor restoration and retention of fences when ownership is uncertain.","Assess predecessor-by-failure-boundary test coverage, concurrent operations, backward journals, stopped completion, rollback integrity and applicable prior lifecycle design constraints. Reassess cutover-01 through cutover-04 without presuming resolution."],"dependsOn":["install"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"visuals","title":"Lifecycle sequence source, generated companion and actual rendering","selectors":["/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","/body/companions","document:line:131"],"concerns":["Inspect the current authored sequence, all participant descriptions, generated companion content and actual rendering where available. Explicitly record any unavailable mandatory rendering verification.","Check controller, predecessor, launchd, supervisor and child responsibilities and message directions against the substantive ownership contracts.","Verify that running and stopped success, conditional predecessor exit, uncommitted failure, candidate reconciliation, prior-state restoration and uncertain-outcome fencing are understandable in the generated visual.","Check whether labels and generated structure express alternative routes rather than misleading sequential execution; do not infer rendered branch behavior from descriptions alone.","Verify the live document hyperlink, canonical companion path and source/generated agreement. Reassess visuals-01 and visuals-02 and the prior rendering limitation without presuming resolution.","Independently assess whether the changed interaction and ownership boundaries require any additional authored artifacts."],"dependsOn":["install","cutover"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"consistency","title":"Fresh whole-artifact requirement and contract consistency","selectors":[],"concerns":["Reconcile all fresh substantive results against the originating ISSUE, including fresh start/restart, supported automatic migration, direct installs, recovery jobs, broker-denied exit, preserved data and running state, interruption qualification and Linux behavior.","Check cross-chunk signatures, release qualification, journal variants, ownership transfer, activation/update ordering, terminal outcome rules, test mappings and dependency feasibility.","Check unchanged context, chosen alternative, open questions and companion metadata for indirect contradictions introduced by the revised design.","Verify canonical/live/generated agreement, citation targets and disposition of every carried finding only after fresh inspection.","Ensure each assigned selector was inspected or explicitly limited; distinguish mandatory missing evidence from optional implementation execution and apply the required final-status precedence."],"dependsOn":["install","cutover","visuals"],"purpose":"consistency"}],"coverageExplanation":"All 36 current inventory units are assigned to substantive chunks. Shared contracts, errors, migration and tests are deliberately assessed under both installer/update integration and cutover/recovery responsibilities. All 14 current citations are covered, including added or renumbered references. The diagram section selector is updated from document:line:89 to document:line:131. Visual source, participant units, companion metadata and rendering receive fresh inspection. The final consistency chunk depends on every substantive chunk and supplies no substitute inventory coverage.","finalConsistencyChunkId":"consistency","coverage":[{"unitId":"/body/summary","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"/body/hldContextSlice","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"/body/contractDetails","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"/body/dataModelChanges","chunkIds":["cutover"]},{"unitId":"/body/interactionWithShared","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"/body/errorPaths","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"/body/testStrategy","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"/body/migration","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"/body/chosenAlternative","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"/body/openQuestions","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/companions","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/0","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"/body/alternativesConsidered/1","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","chunkIds":["visuals"]},{"unitId":"/citations/0","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"/citations/1","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/2","chunkIds":["cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/3","chunkIds":["cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/4","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/5","chunkIds":["cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/6","chunkIds":["cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/7","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/8","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/9","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/10","chunkIds":["cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/11","chunkIds":["cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/12","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"/citations/13","chunkIds":["install","cutover"]},{"unitId":"document:line:25","chunkIds":["install"]},{"unitId":"document:line:131","chunkIds":["visuals"]}]},"impact":{"baselineAttempt":1,"mode":"full","changes":["Compared the published attempt 1 baseline, accepted plan and completed feedback with attempt 2's captured content and current live files. The live document matches the attempt 2 captured document, and the live canonical body matches its captured canonical body.","The summary and alternatives now center on a staged bridge, immutable releases and fencing the canonical legacy entry before shutdown.","stageManagedInstallation is described as staging-only, with controller-owned activation reservation, explicit start intent, partial-publication journaling and idle/running settlement.","A launchManagedUpdate contract adds running managed RPC helper routing, acknowledgement ordering, stopped local updates and omission of the legacy self-shutdown timer.","The data model now specifies activation reservations, tagged predecessor variants, historical decoding, direct rollback recipes, recovery-job metadata, release qualification provenance and launcher-fence evidence.","Error handling and migration introduce atomic checkout-entry exchange, old-helper admission checks, run-file guard transfer, drain classifications and durable-outcome recovery that distinguishes committed success from uncommitted failure.","The test strategy and acceptance mapping now include client routing, release provenance, competing legacy operations, startup guard transfer, drain classification and uncertain publication.","The sequence participants and messages changed to describe running/stopped routes and rollback/fencing. Companion metadata remains unchanged, so link correctness and generated/rendered agreement still require fresh verification.","Citations expanded from nine to fourteen and were renumbered; the diagram section moved from document:line:89 to document:line:131."],"directChunkIds":["install","cutover","visuals"],"indirectChunkIds":[],"rationale":"Every current substantive chunk contains direct material changes, so all three are selected once in directChunkIds; none is duplicated in indirectChunkIds. The same changes also affect unchanged requirements and shared interfaces: guarded launcher delivery constrains predecessor admission and rollback, activation intent constrains idle/readiness verification, release qualification constrains early-exit recovery, and terminal outcome semantics constrain both prose and visuals. These indirect effects are included in the selected chunks and fresh final consistency. Attempt 1 was fully published but its overall assessment and visual coverage were incomplete; its install and cutover results also concern contracts now materially revised. No prior result is retained, no earlier pass is substituted, and all ten accepted findings remain carried pending fresh inspection. The originating ISSUE remains the required workflow ancestor; the earlier lifecycle LLD is applicable supporting contract evidence, not invented HLD ancestry.","uncertainReason":"The prior actual-rendering limitation remains unresolved at preparation time. Full fresh coverage avoids relying on that incomplete result or assuming that revised source establishes a correct rendering.","chunkMapping":[{"priorIds":["install"],"currentIds":["install"],"explanation":"Retains the installer/update responsibility and stable chunk ID, but expands migration coverage and updates citation selectors and concerns for activation, release provisioning and managed update routing. All coverage is fresh."},{"priorIds":["cutover"],"currentIds":["cutover"],"explanation":"Retains predecessor/transaction/recovery responsibility and dependency on install. Revised variants, fencing, guard transfer, exit classification and durable recovery require fresh assessment, with updated citations."},{"priorIds":["visuals"],"currentIds":["visuals"],"explanation":"Retains visual responsibility and dependencies on install and cutover. Replaces the retired document:line:89 selector with document:line:131 and reassesses changed source, generated content, links and rendering. Prior incomplete coverage is not retained."},{"priorIds":["consistency"],"currentIds":["consistency"],"explanation":"Retains the final consistency role and dependencies on all substantive chunks, but always executes it freshly. No substantive chunks were added, removed or merged."}],"retainedCoverage":[],"carriedFindingIds":["[1,\"install\",\"install-01\"]","[1,\"install\",\"install-02\"]","[1,\"install\",\"install-03\"]","[1,\"install\",\"install-04\"]","[1,\"cutover\",\"cutover-01\"]","[1,\"cutover\",\"cutover-02\"]","[1,\"cutover\",\"cutover-03\"]","[1,\"cutover\",\"cutover-04\"]","[1,\"visuals\",\"visuals-01\"]","[1,\"visuals\",\"visuals-02\"]"],"consistencyChunkIds":["consistency"]},"unitSummaries":[{"unitId":"impact","phase":"impact","automaticDispatches":2,"retriesUsed":1,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[{"code":"invalid_output","summary":"Selected substantive IDs are unknown or overlapping"}],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"install","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"cutover","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"visuals","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":2,"retriesUsed":1,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[{"code":"invalid_output","summary":"Resolution requires accepted fresh inspection without mandatory gaps"}],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6","attempt":2,"artifactId":"LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1","status":"incomplete","counts":{"HIGH":2,"MED":8,"LOW":2},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"install","status":"incomplete","summary":"The revision addresses the substance of install-01 through install-04: supported first-upgrade routes, immutable release provisioning, controller-owned activation, and running/stopped managed updates are now described. One managed-update acknowledgement ordering defect remains. Diagram source was inspected, but rendering verification was unavailable.","findings":[{"id":"install-05","severity":"MED","location":"LLD.md:78-98; /body/contractDetails/api/2","message":"The running managed update prepares the candidate before launching the transactional helper and returning its acknowledgement. Candidate preparation includes fetching, dependency installation and building, which can exceed the existing client’s 20-second reply deadline. That deadline destroys the socket, causing the response-written handshake to fail and preventing the helper from proceeding. Moving preparation into the helper before its reservation acknowledgement also conflicts with the existing 15-second launch timeout. Define a bounded launch acknowledgement followed by detached preparation before any shutdown, or explicitly revise the client/helper timing contract. Add coverage where preparation exceeds both current deadlines; otherwise ordinary managed updates can repeatedly cancel on slow builds.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:95","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:208","src/shared/ipc-client.ts:77-100,244","src/daemon/managed-update-launch.ts:20,40-55,78-88","src/daemon/server.ts:395-418","vscode-plugin/src/freshness/daemon-freshness.ts:202-217"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/hldContextSlice","document:line:25","/body/contractDetails","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/0","/citations/1","/citations/4","/citations/7","/citations/8","/citations/9","/citations/12","/citations/13","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-5d5478c61a25ac8f.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: prior install-01 through install-04 feedback","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html: Mermaid source and rendering shell","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh","scripts/daemon-ctl.sh","src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts","src/shared/update-source.ts","src/shared/ipc-client.ts:65-105,244-245","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-launch.ts","src/daemon/release-compatibility.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts:264-350","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts:97-122","src/daemon/update-runner.ts:135-200","src/daemon/server.ts:380-445","src/cli/services/maintenance.ts:108-263,373-420","vscode-plugin/src/daemon/controller.ts","vscode-plugin/src/freshness/daemon-freshness.ts:175-245","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/lifecycle/DaemonLifecycleCommandRunner.kt","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/daemon/DaemonGateway.kt:1389-1410"],"limitations":["Could not visually verify docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html: opening the artifact returned 'The browser access host is unavailable'. Its Mermaid source was inspected, but no actual rendering was verified."],"advice":["Make the configured-source route tests assert custom repository URL, branch and installation root preservation across installer, shell, TUI and both IDE entry points."]},{"chunkId":"cutover","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The revised design addresses predecessor variants, release qualification, drain uncertainty and durable-success recovery. Two material gaps remain: the controller-to-supervisor guard handoff lacks an implementable recovery contract, and rollback does not preserve a previously registered but stopped legacy job.","findings":[{"id":"cutover-r2-01","severity":"MED","location":"/body/migration/steps/3; LLD.md:210; /body/errorPaths/errorCases/0","message":"The uninterrupted guard handoff is stated as an invariant but has no adoption interface or durable transition contract. Existing quiescence checks reject any run-file guard, SupervisorRunFiles.prepare creates a new guard and rejects an existing one, and child borrowing requires the owner record to name its supervisor. Keeping the controller's guard therefore prevents the existing handoff/start path; releasing it permits the excluded legacy startup race. Define authenticated adoption, owner-record and local-handle invalidation, journaled transfer evidence, and recovery when either process dies before or after adoption. Include settlement for a stopped update, where no child startup occurs, and guard disposition before legacy rollback. Test failures on both sides of each transfer boundary.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:140-141","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:209-212","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts:65-112","src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts:requireQuiescentInstallation","src/daemon/supervisor-run-files.ts:49-110","src/bin/insrc-daemon-supervisor.ts:allowInitialStart","src/daemon/managed-update-handoff.ts:effects.inspectStores and stageManagedCandidate"]},{"id":"cutover-r2-02","severity":"MED","location":"/body/errorPaths/errorCases/3/response; LLD.md:153; /body/dataModelChanges/1","message":"Rollback restores the previous job or direct launch only if it was running, although legacy-stopped explicitly permits a pinned idle job. After that job is removed for migration, this rule leaves a previously registered stopped installation without its job. Restoring registration must be separate from deciding whether to launch a child. Also retain or replace the existing refusal of a stopped job with RunAtLoad=true: bootstrapping its exact descriptor starts a daemon and violates stopped-state preservation. Specify these branches and cover rollback after job removal for stopped predecessors with both descriptor policies.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:113","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:151-154","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md:Fix intent","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts:migrate stopped-install RunAtLoad refusal","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts:141-175","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts:completeLegacyMigration"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/migration","/body/testStrategy","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/7","/citations/8","/citations/9","/citations/10","/citations/11","/citations/12","/citations/13","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: prior cutover-01 through cutover-04 and current chunk inventory","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/restore-reliable-daemon-restart-macos-E202611103992d2e1/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-3992d2e1e26124dc.json","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts","src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-handoff.ts","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts","src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts","src/daemon/release-compatibility.ts","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts","src/bin/insrc-daemon-supervisor.ts","src/daemon/supervisor-run-files.ts","src/daemon/managed-daemon-lifecycle.ts","src/daemon/run-file-ownership.ts","src/daemon/index.ts: startup, store opening and readiness","src/daemon/server.ts: guarded close","src/daemon/update-runner.ts: legacy update launch","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts: shutdown and update routing","src/daemon/shutdown.ts","scripts/daemon-ctl.sh","src/daemon/__tests__/legacy-daemon-cutover.test.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Expand the proposed recovery tests into a predecessor-by-failure-boundary matrix, including interrupted checkout exchange, guard adoption, candidate registration, provisional selection and terminal publication.","Document the concrete supported direct-launch environment recipe and accepted recovery-job loader argv alongside the qualification metadata so admission fixtures can verify exact values."]},{"chunkId":"visuals","status":"incomplete","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector, all five participant descriptions, the generated companion, issue requirements and relevant lifecycle code. The revised sequence adds outcome labels but still presents mutually exclusive routes sequentially. The companion hyperlink remains broken. Actual rendering could not be verified.","findings":[{"id":"visuals-03","severity":"MED","location":"/body/sequenceDefinition/messages/2–11; sequence-diagram.html embedded sequenceDiagram","message":"The revised labels partially address visuals-01, but the generated Mermaid still contains one linear sequence with no conditional or alternative structure. It shows running startup/readiness followed by stopped-state idle verification, then committed success followed by candidate reconciliation and rollback. It also leaves verified predecessor exit unconditional after a conditional exit request. These mutually exclusive routes contradict the lifecycle contract, particularly the prohibition on rolling back durable success. Represent conditional predecessor exit, running versus stopped completion, and uncommitted failure versus committed success as explicit alternatives in the generated visual; distinguish uncertain publication recovery before deciding whether rollback is permitted.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json: /body/sequenceDefinition/messages/2–11","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html: embedded sequenceDiagram contains all twelve arrows without opt/alt/else blocks","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:151–157,164–165,210–212","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md: Fix intent","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts:96–108 requireReady","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts: finish, settleManagedUpdate, recoverManagedTransaction"]},{"id":"visuals-04","severity":"LOW","location":"docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:133","message":"The hyperlink still repeats the repository-relative document directory. Resolving it relative to LLD.md produces a nonexistent nested path, although the canonical companion exists. This leaves visuals-02 unresolved. Use sequence-diagram.html as the document-relative target or a supported repository-root link.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:133",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json: /body/companions/0/relPath","Filesystem verification: canonical companion exists; document-relative resolution of the current hyperlink does not"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","/body/companions","document:line:131","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts: requireReady, completeLegacyMigration, Rollback candidate reconciliation","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts","src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts","src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts: registerManagedJob, removeManagedJob"],"limitations":["Actual rendering of docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html remains unverified: opening the companion through the browser tool returned 'The browser access host is unavailable'. Source and generated Mermaid were inspected, but layout, clipping and successful runtime rendering were not verified."],"advice":["The participant descriptions distinguish controller, predecessor, supervisor and child responsibilities, but descriptions are omitted from the generated Mermaid. Consider separating launchd from the predecessor and supervisor, showing registration/removal against launchd and exact-exit observation as a controller operation. Currently 'Verified exit' appears as a predecessor response, and 'register job' targets the supervisor itself.","The generated participant and message labels agree with the authored source, and the canonical companion path is correct. A corrected sequence together with the existing ownership/cardinality prose is sufficient; no additional ERD or UX artifact is necessary for these interaction changes."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"incomplete","summary":"Reconciled all three accepted fresh substantive reviews against the originating ISSUE and current canonical/live documents. All assigned substantive selectors have coverage declarations. Remaining concerns are already recorded in install-05, cutover-r2-01, cutover-r2-02, visuals-03 and visuals-04; no additional finding is duplicated here. Mandatory rendering verification remains outstanding, preventing a complete assessment.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-5d5478c61a25ac8f.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html: embedded Mermaid and companion metadata","docs/standalone/restore-reliable-daemon-restart-macos-E202611103992d2e1/S001/LLD.md: sections 3.3, 3.4 and 7","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts: UpdatePredecessor, validPredecessor and recovery classification","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts","src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts: stageManagedInstallation","src/shared/ipc-client.ts: RPC deadlines and update client","src/daemon/managed-update-launch.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts: completeLegacyMigration and recoverInstalledManagedUpdate","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts","src/daemon/release-compatibility.ts","src/daemon/supervisor-run-files.ts","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts","src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts: update routing","src/daemon/server.ts: update response-written handshake","src/daemon/shutdown.ts: watchdog failure and drain completion","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts: staging and legacy migration"],"limitations":["Mandatory actual rendering verification of docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html remains outstanding. Accepted attempt-2 install and visuals feedback records an unavailable browser access host. This consistency inspection verified embedded source and canonical agreement, but did not establish runtime rendering, layout or clipping. Those fresh chunks remain incomplete; their earlier findings are carried rather than declared resolved."],"advice":["Address the existing fresh findings without duplicating them: install-05 concerns preparation versus acknowledgement deadlines; cutover-r2-01 concerns recoverable guard adoption; cutover-r2-02 concerns restoring stopped-job registration; visuals-03 and visuals-04 concern alternative branches and the broken companion link.","The captured attempt-2 canonical body and live document match current files. Generated participant/message labels match the authored sequence, all fourteen citation targets exist, and companion metadata identifies the existing file. Source agreement does not establish visual correctness.","The ISSUE's fresh activation, supported first upgrade, direct/recovery-job migration, broker-denied exit, data preservation and Linux requirements are represented in the revised prose and proposed test subjects. Remaining end-to-end feasibility concerns are captured by the accepted fresh findings. The chosen bridge alternative and empty open-question list introduce no additional independent contradiction.","Label ac1–ac3 with the corresponding ISSUE fix-intent requirements, and expand interruption qualification into predecessor-by-boundary cases covering checkout exchange, guard transfer, job removal, candidate admission and terminal publication. Executing implementation tests is outside this design assessment."],"findingDecisions":[{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"install","findingId":"install-01"},"rationale":"The revision now names updated IDE, shell/TUI and standard-installer first-upgrade routes, including older-caller fallback. However, accepted fresh install inspection is incomplete, so this origin remains carried pending inspection without mandatory gaps.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:167,207–214",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/install, status and limitations"],"action":"carry"},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"install","findingId":"install-02"},"rationale":"Immutable release roots, predecessor preservation, trusted qualification and missing-declaration allowlists are now described. Formal resolution remains withheld because the accepted fresh install chunk has a mandatory verification gap.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:121–129,208",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/install"],"action":"carry"},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"install","findingId":"install-03"},"rationale":"The revised contract separates staging-only behavior from controller-owned activation and records explicit start intent and partial-publication recovery. The accepted fresh install assessment remains incomplete, so this origin is not closed.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:34–54,102–109,164",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/install"],"action":"carry"},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"install","findingId":"install-04"},"rationale":"Running managed RPC and stopped external-controller routes are now specified, but the accepted fresh install review is incomplete and identifies a remaining acknowledgement-ordering defect in install-05. Preserve this origin rather than claim completed resolution.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:78–98,165,211",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/install/findings/install-05 and limitations","src/daemon/managed-update-launch.ts: launchManagedUpdate and waitForReservation","src/shared/ipc-client.ts: createDaemonClient.update"],"action":"carry"},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"cutover","findingId":"cutover-01"},"rationale":"Fresh cutover inspection has no mandatory gaps. The revised model defines all four predecessor variants, required identity and rollback evidence, selector absence/baseline, historical decoding and rejection rules. Recovery-job loader admission is explicitly constrained. The separately identified stopped-job restoration defect remains in cutover-r2-02.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:111–119,143–145",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json: /body/dataModelChanges/1",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/cutover","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts: UpdatePredecessor and validPredecessor","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts: verifyLegacyService"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["cutover"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"cutover","findingId":"cutover-02"},"rationale":"Canonical launcher exchange and old-helper exclusion materially improve admission, but uninterrupted exclusion still depends on an undefined controller-to-supervisor guard adoption. Fresh cutover-r2-01 demonstrates that the existing acquisition and borrowing contracts cannot perform the promised handoff. Preserve the original exclusion concern.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:139–141,209–210",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/cutover/findings/cutover-r2-01","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts: acquireRunFileGuard and borrowRunFileGuard","src/daemon/supervisor-run-files.ts: acquire and prepare","docs/standalone/restore-reliable-daemon-restart-macos-E202611103992d2e1/S001/LLD.md: migration step 1"],"action":"carry"},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"cutover","findingId":"cutover-03"},"rationale":"Fresh cutover inspection has no mandatory gaps. The revision separates precommit candidate failures from uncertain outcome publication, requires rereading the matching durable result, forbids rollback of committed success and distinguishes provisional selection from terminal publication. This matches the existing transaction contract.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:75–76,151–157,211–212","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts: finish and recoverManagedTransaction","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts: recoverInstalledManagedUpdate",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/cutover"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["cutover"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"cutover","findingId":"cutover-04"},"rationale":"Fresh cutover inspection has no mandatory gaps. The revision now persists graceful, broker-denied or unknown classification, requires correlated positive evidence for the first two, treats unavailable proof as unknown, requires crash-consistent release qualification for nongraceful reopening and reports classification to the user. Proposed qualification includes clean-drain and regression predecessors.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:113,147–150,182–187","src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts: drainLegacyDaemonForCutover","src/daemon/shutdown.ts: failClosed and drain completion",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/cutover"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["cutover"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"visuals","findingId":"visuals-01"},"rationale":"The revised generated sequence still expresses mutually exclusive running, stopped, success and rollback routes as one linear sequence. Accepted visuals-03 confirms the continuing concern, and actual rendering remains unverified. Carry this origin.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json: /body/sequenceDefinition/messages","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html: embedded sequenceDiagram",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/visuals"],"action":"carry"},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"visuals","findingId":"visuals-02"},"rationale":"The live hyperlink still repeats the repository-relative directory and resolves to a nonexistent document-relative target. The canonical companion exists. Accepted visuals-04 confirms this unchanged defect; no resolution is claimed.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:133",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json: /body/companions/0/relPath",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/visuals/findings/visuals-04"],"action":"carry"}]}],"limitations":["Could not visually verify docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html: opening the artifact returned 'The browser access host is unavailable'. Its Mermaid source was inspected, but no actual rendering was verified.","Actual rendering of docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html remains unverified: opening the companion through the browser tool returned 'The browser access host is unavailable'. Source and generated Mermaid were inspected, but layout, clipping and successful runtime rendering were not verified.","Mandatory actual rendering verification of docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html remains outstanding. Accepted attempt-2 install and visuals feedback records an unavailable browser access host. This consistency inspection verified embedded source and canonical agreement, but did not establish runtime rendering, layout or clipping. Those fresh chunks remain incomplete; their earlier findings are carried rather than declared resolved."],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"0836a5530af73b66da092db6ccd4ea4df8e636f409ff0a491cc94947f9eb8904","impact":{"baselineAttempt":1,"mode":"full","coverageOrigins":[{"chunkId":"install","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"cutover","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"visuals","kind":"fresh"},{"chunkId":"consistency","kind":"fresh"}],"findingDecisions":[{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"install","findingId":"install-01"},"rationale":"The revision now names updated IDE, shell/TUI and standard-installer first-upgrade routes, including older-caller fallback. However, accepted fresh install inspection is incomplete, so this origin remains carried pending inspection without mandatory gaps.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:167,207–214",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/install, status and limitations"],"action":"carry"},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"install","findingId":"install-02"},"rationale":"Immutable release roots, predecessor preservation, trusted qualification and missing-declaration allowlists are now described. Formal resolution remains withheld because the accepted fresh install chunk has a mandatory verification gap.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:121–129,208",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/install"],"action":"carry"},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"install","findingId":"install-03"},"rationale":"The revised contract separates staging-only behavior from controller-owned activation and records explicit start intent and partial-publication recovery. The accepted fresh install assessment remains incomplete, so this origin is not closed.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:34–54,102–109,164",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/install"],"action":"carry"},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"install","findingId":"install-04"},"rationale":"Running managed RPC and stopped external-controller routes are now specified, but the accepted fresh install review is incomplete and identifies a remaining acknowledgement-ordering defect in install-05. Preserve this origin rather than claim completed resolution.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:78–98,165,211",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/install/findings/install-05 and limitations","src/daemon/managed-update-launch.ts: launchManagedUpdate and waitForReservation","src/shared/ipc-client.ts: createDaemonClient.update"],"action":"carry"},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"cutover","findingId":"cutover-01"},"rationale":"Fresh cutover inspection has no mandatory gaps. The revised model defines all four predecessor variants, required identity and rollback evidence, selector absence/baseline, historical decoding and rejection rules. Recovery-job loader admission is explicitly constrained. The separately identified stopped-job restoration defect remains in cutover-r2-02.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:111–119,143–145",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json: /body/dataModelChanges/1",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/cutover","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts: UpdatePredecessor and validPredecessor","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts: verifyLegacyService"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["cutover"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"cutover","findingId":"cutover-02"},"rationale":"Canonical launcher exchange and old-helper exclusion materially improve admission, but uninterrupted exclusion still depends on an undefined controller-to-supervisor guard adoption. Fresh cutover-r2-01 demonstrates that the existing acquisition and borrowing contracts cannot perform the promised handoff. Preserve the original exclusion concern.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:139–141,209–210",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/cutover/findings/cutover-r2-01","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts: acquireRunFileGuard and borrowRunFileGuard","src/daemon/supervisor-run-files.ts: acquire and prepare","docs/standalone/restore-reliable-daemon-restart-macos-E202611103992d2e1/S001/LLD.md: migration step 1"],"action":"carry"},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"cutover","findingId":"cutover-03"},"rationale":"Fresh cutover inspection has no mandatory gaps. The revision separates precommit candidate failures from uncertain outcome publication, requires rereading the matching durable result, forbids rollback of committed success and distinguishes provisional selection from terminal publication. This matches the existing transaction contract.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:75–76,151–157,211–212","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts: finish and recoverManagedTransaction","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts: recoverInstalledManagedUpdate",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/cutover"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["cutover"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"cutover","findingId":"cutover-04"},"rationale":"Fresh cutover inspection has no mandatory gaps. The revision now persists graceful, broker-denied or unknown classification, requires correlated positive evidence for the first two, treats unavailable proof as unknown, requires crash-consistent release qualification for nongraceful reopening and reports classification to the user. Proposed qualification includes clean-drain and regression predecessors.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:113,147–150,182–187","src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts: drainLegacyDaemonForCutover","src/daemon/shutdown.ts: failClosed and drain completion",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/cutover"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["cutover"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"visuals","findingId":"visuals-01"},"rationale":"The revised generated sequence still expresses mutually exclusive running, stopped, success and rollback routes as one linear sequence. Accepted visuals-03 confirms the continuing concern, and actual rendering remains unverified. Carry this origin.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json: /body/sequenceDefinition/messages","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html: embedded sequenceDiagram",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/visuals"],"action":"carry"},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"visuals","findingId":"visuals-02"},"rationale":"The live hyperlink still repeats the repository-relative directory and resolves to a nonexistent document-relative target. The canonical companion exists. Accepted visuals-04 confirms this unchanged defect; no resolution is claimed.","evidenceReferences":["LLD.md:133",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json: /body/companions/0/relPath",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-installer-migration-5d5478c6.json: attempt 2 completedChunks/visuals/findings/visuals-04"],"action":"carry"}],"effectiveFindingOrigins":[{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"install","findingId":"install-01"},{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"install","findingId":"install-02"},{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"install","findingId":"install-03"},{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"install","findingId":"install-04"},{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"cutover","findingId":"cutover-02"},{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"visuals","findingId":"visuals-01"},{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"visuals","findingId":"visuals-02"},{"attempt":2,"chunkId":"install","findingId":"install-05"},{"attempt":2,"chunkId":"cutover","findingId":"cutover-r2-01"},{"attempt":2,"chunkId":"cutover","findingId":"cutover-r2-02"},{"attempt":2,"chunkId":"visuals","findingId":"visuals-03"},{"attempt":2,"chunkId":"visuals","findingId":"visuals-04"}]}},"finishedAt":"2026-11-11T16:51:02.469Z"}]}}}}
991	{"artifactId":"LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1","entry":{"id":"56d44052b8744f1fb933c3ee2a02e5b8","actor":{"id":"insrc:approval","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:53:38.373Z","operation":"approve","revision":{"number":2,"contentHash":"abc5eb009b462bf0a67fbb2f09474ce6399e2cb73d9ada068adfb266a7f8b943"},"status":{"from":"draft","to":"approved"},"outcome":{"result":"override","summary":"The user explicitly approved the whole design-review override after presentation, including the open functional findings. Waive independent visual verification and accept the unresolved design findings for update acknowledgement timing before detached preparation, journaled run-file guard transfer and recovery, and restoration of a previously registered stopped LaunchAgent without starting its daemon. The review also carries earlier findings because verification was incomplete. Local rendering was verified; the generated linear diagram does not express mutually exclusive paths."}}}
