[]},{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6","attempt":1,"artifactId":"LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1","status":"incomplete","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":4,"LOW":1},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"passed","summary":"The assigned scope and design choices align with the originating ISSUE. Fresh installation, supported updates, legacy and recovery jobs, direct installs, broker denial, rollback preservation and Linux compatibility are traced into the design and test strategy. The cited BUILD supports the motivation for portable qualification without establishing completed production qualification. No blocking defect was demonstrated in this chunk.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/hldContextSlice","/body/summary","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/13","/citations/16","document:line:25","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md:5-15",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-5d5478c61a25ac8f.json",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-3992d2e1e26124dc.json",".insrc/artifacts/BUILD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json:body.summary","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/TESTS.md:174-232","src/daemon/managed-release-staging.ts:99-153","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:164-225",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6.json"],"limitations":[],"advice":["The rendered summary still displays Epic and HLD metadata despite the explicit standalone context. Labeling these as framework bookkeeping would make the ISSUE ancestry clearer."]},{"chunkId":"qualification","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned sections and citations were inspected against the originating ISSUE and current implementation. The design establishes appropriate qualification and rollback invariants, but leaves the native equivalence mechanism and trust lifecycle insufficiently specified for implementation.","findings":[{"id":"qualification-native-verifier","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/0/postconditions","message":"The central portable-build mechanism remains a requirement rather than a concrete design. The LLD requires independently reconstructed native bytes and permits only proven non-semantic differences, but supplies no supported initial toolchain profile, verifier operations, reconstruction algorithm, or inventory rules that can accept the observed independently built native variants. The cited implementation only compares whole-tree fingerprints; it has no native equivalence mechanism to inherit. Its build also inherits compiler/environment inputs, while .npmrc permits both prebuilt and source-built dependencies. Specify the initial supported build inputs, complete runtime inventory, allowed native transformations and independent reference-generation procedure, together with positive variance and negative modification cases. Otherwise implementations can satisfy fail-closed rejection while still rejecting the ordinary source-built installs this change is intended to migrate.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:52-54","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:175-179","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:192","src/daemon/managed-release-staging.ts:fingerprint, stageManagedRelease","build-process-broker.mjs:16-19",".npmrc","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-release-staging.test.ts:fixture"]},{"id":"qualification-trust-lifecycle","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/0/preconditions; /body/dataModelChanges/2; /body/errorPaths/errorCases/5","message":"The trust lifecycle does not define how an updater determines that signed evidence is stale or revoked, or how that decision interacts with offline recovery. Shipping a trust key and requiring scoped rotation/revocation does not specify a trusted key-set format, revocation source, freshness or replay rule, or whether an already admitted transaction retains its authorization after key rotation or revocation. The current note reader checks source and commit only, and the durable compatibility receipt contains release-format declarations rather than a trust snapshot. Define the authenticated trust-state distribution, freshness policy, and durable receipt fields and recovery rules, including expiry or revocation between preparation, cutover and offline rollback. Add tests for those boundaries. Without this contract, implementations can either accept replayed authorization or strand an interrupted update by requiring unavailable remote evidence.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:49","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:101","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:137-140","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:200","src/daemon/managed-update-preparation.ts:originQualification","src/daemon/managed-update-handoff.ts:97-108","src/daemon/release-compatibility.ts:qualifiedPairFromReservation"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/9","/citations/14","/citations/15","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","src/daemon/managed-release-staging.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-preparation.ts","src/daemon/release-compatibility.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-handoff.ts:1-175","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts:1-215","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts:1-125","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-release-staging.test.ts:1-120","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/TESTS.md:155-232","build-process-broker.mjs",".npmrc","package.json","copy-assets.mjs"],"limitations":[],"advice":["The proposed real-production-build promotion matrix appropriately exceeds the existing synthetic staging fixtures. Preserve that distinction when reporting qualification results; existing fixture passes do not establish native portability."]},{"chunkId":"lifecycle","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The assigned lifecycle sections cover activation, predecessor identification, drain classification, guard transfer and durable recovery. Rollback ordering reopens legacy mutation before the transaction has verified restoration and published its terminal outcome.","findings":[{"id":"lifecycle-rollback-launcher-fence","severity":"MED","location":"/body/errorPaths/errorCases/3/response; /body/migration/steps/6","message":"Rollback restores the canonical legacy launcher before restoring and verifying the previous service and publishing the durable rollback outcome. This re-enables precisely the old commands that the design says cannot honor the new reservation. A concurrent old restart, updater or installer can therefore enter during rollback, disrupt the restored service or mutate the pinned checkout; an interruption after launcher restoration also leaves an active reservation without its launcher fence. The cited recovery implementation follows this ordering: it settles the guard, restores the launcher, then restores the service, with outcome publication afterward. Keep legacy mutation fenced through verified restoration and durable outcome publication, defining a restricted rollback launch route or equivalent mechanism that can start the predecessor without reopening ordinary old commands. Add concurrent-operation and interruption tests at this boundary.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:118","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:131","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:206","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts:Rollback.run, rollback-legacy-service","src/daemon/legacy-cutover-admission.ts:restoreLegacyLauncher","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts:settleManagedUpdate","src/daemon/update-runner.ts:resolveDaemonCtl, isUpdateInProgress"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/10","/citations/11","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts","src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts","src/daemon/legacy-cutover-admission.ts","src/daemon/legacy-run-guard.ts","src/daemon/legacy-drain-evidence.ts","src/daemon/fresh-managed-activation.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-handoff.ts","src/daemon/managed-daemon-probation.ts","src/daemon/index.ts:startup and shutdown lifecycle","src/daemon/shutdown.ts","src/daemon/update-runner.ts:legacy helper launch and update marker","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-handoff.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/fresh-managed-activation.test.ts:activation recovery scenarios","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-transaction.test.ts:test inventory","src/daemon/__tests__/legacy-cutover-admission.test.ts:test inventory","src/daemon/__tests__/legacy-run-guard.test.ts:test inventory"],"limitations":[],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"entrypoints","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The assigned sections cover installer/client routing, explicit start intent, older-client limitations, Linux preservation and release promotion tests. The first-upgrade bootstrap path leaves a gap in the required verification-before-execution trust boundary.","findings":[{"id":"entrypoints-bootstrap-before-verification","severity":"MED","location":"/body/migration/migrationSteps/1; /body/migration/migrationSteps/2","message":"The design routes first upgrades through the current standard installer but does not replace its unverified bridge bootstrap. That installer clones the configured branch, runs its npm installation/build instructions, and executes its newly built controller before prepareLegacyUpgrade fetches qualification evidence. Consequently, an unsigned or unauthorized configured source can execute code before stageManagedRelease enforces the stated rule that a source override grants no signing authority. Building outside the incumbent root does not constrain that code's access to the incumbent or user data. Specify a trusted bootstrap controller/verifier distributed with the installer or clients, and authenticate the exact bridge source before executing its build instructions or controller. Add an entrypoint test proving invalid or missing authorization prevents bridge execution.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:201","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:202","LLD /body/contractDetails/api/0/preconditions/0","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:217","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:218","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:223","src/daemon/managed-update-preparation.ts:prepareLegacyUpgrade, stageRelease, originQualification","src/daemon/__tests__/macos-upgrade-routing.test.ts:requireBridge"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/0","/citations/7","/citations/8","/citations/12","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/TESTS.md","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh","scripts/daemon-ctl.sh","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts","src/daemon/update-runner.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-preparation.ts","src/daemon/index.ts:managed update dispatch","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts:activation, migration, dispatch and update entrypoints","src/shared/update-source.ts","src/cli/services/maintenance.ts:update","src/cli/services/daemon.ts:lifecycle call sites","vscode-plugin/src/daemon/controller.ts","vscode-plugin/src/daemon/commands.ts","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:freshness wiring","vscode-plugin/src/freshness/daemon-freshness.ts:performUpdate and confirmUpdate","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/lifecycle/DaemonLifecycleService.kt:DefaultDaemonScriptLocator","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/lifecycle/ScriptDaemonProvisioner.kt","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/lifecycle/DaemonLifecycleCommandRunner.kt","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/freshness/InstalledCommitFreshnessConsumer.kt:production wiring","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/freshness/DaemonFreshnessFlow.kt:performUpdate","src/daemon/__tests__/macos-upgrade-routing.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-release-staging.test.ts:fixture and scenario inventory","src/daemon/__tests__/linux-installed-lifecycle.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/fixtures/linux-installed-lifecycle.sh"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Specify how installer/controller outcome details reach IDE users while preserving existing result shapes. Current lifecycle adapters reduce nonzero exits to generic errors, obscuring verified rollback versus fenced uncertainty.","Keep synthetic routing/staging fixture results distinct from the newly required production-build promotion evidence. Test execution was not needed for this read-only design assessment."]},{"chunkId":"visuals","status":"incomplete","summary":"Inspected the complete sequence, all six participant descriptions, companion HTML and document reference against the lifecycle requirements. The generated source preserves the authored content. Actual rendering could not be verified. Relationship ownership is adequately described in prose; no additional ERD or UX mock is necessary.","findings":[{"id":"visuals-relative-companion-link","severity":"LOW","location":"docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:111","message":"The sequence link repeats the repository-relative directory inside a document already located in that directory. Standard Markdown resolution therefore points to a nonexistent nested path. Use sequence-diagram.html relative to LLD.md so readers can open the existing companion.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:111","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html","Filesystem check: document-relative target absent; repository-relative companion present."]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/5","/body/companions","document:line:109","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6.json"],"limitations":["Mandatory visual verification of /Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html could not be completed: the browser tool reported that its access host is unavailable. HTML, Mermaid source and participant/message descriptions were inspected, but rendered legibility, clipping and layout remain unverified."],"advice":["Represent running versus stopped and success versus uncommitted failure as explicit alternative branches when the sequence format supports them. Current labels and descriptions convey the conditions, but the generated Mermaid places success before rollback in one numbered sequence; branch grouping would clarify the commit boundary and fenced uncertainty."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"incomplete","summary":"Reconciled all five completed chunks against the current LLD and originating ISSUE. Every inventory selector has recorded inspection coverage, and current document and canonical fingerprints match the reviewed baseline. No additional cross-section defect was demonstrated. Existing MED findings remain applicable; mandatory rendered-diagram verification remains incomplete.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json","Checkpoint attempt 1: inventory and accepted completed feedback for scope, qualification, lifecycle, entrypoints and visuals","LLD.md:49-54, 81-107, 117-160, 168-208","Canonical LLD: /body/sequenceDefinition, /body/companions","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:164-223","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts:168-241","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts:18-45"],"limitations":["Mandatory rendering verification remains outstanding for /Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html. The accepted visuals feedback records an unavailable browser access host; source inspection does not establish rendered legibility, clipping or layout."],"advice":["Retain qualification-native-verifier and qualification-trust-lifecycle: they jointly govern whether ordinary independently built predecessors can qualify and whether their authorization remains usable during offline recovery.","Retain entrypoints-bootstrap-before-verification: the installer bridge must obey the same verification-before-execution contract as release staging.","Retain lifecycle-rollback-launcher-fence across recovery prose, implementation contracts, tests and sequence descriptions; restoration must preserve exclusivity through verified restoration and durable outcome publication.","Retain visuals-relative-companion-link and the existing optional diagram branch-grouping advice. No additional ERD or UX artifact requirement was demonstrated.","Keep synthetic fixture results distinct from the proposed real macOS production-build qualification evidence."]}],"limitations":["Mandatory visual verification of /Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html could not be completed: the browser tool reported that its access host is unavailable. HTML, Mermaid source and participant/message descriptions were inspected, but rendered legibility, clipping and layout remain unverified.","Mandatory rendering verification remains outstanding for /Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html. The accepted visuals feedback records an unavailable browser access host; source inspection does not establish rendered legibility, clipping or layout."],"reviewer":"daemon","reviewedContentIdentity":"f7abd2f2be6bedd6765d93a1168c16646720944e1c75e1f3f22411a5b15e7974"},"finishedAt":"2026-11-12T19:44:06.060Z"}]}}}}
