s":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"scope","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"qualification","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"lifecycle","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"entrypoints","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"visuals","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":1,"retriesUsed":0,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[],"actionIds":[]},{"unitId":"consistency","phase":"chunk_review","automaticDispatches":2,"retriesUsed":1,"userDirectedDispatches":0,"diagnostics":[{"code":"invalid_output","summary":"Resolution requires accepted fresh inspection without mandatory gaps"}],"actionIds":[]}],"report":{"reviewId":"macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6","attempt":2,"artifactId":"LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1","status":"incomplete","counts":{"HIGH":0,"MED":3,"LOW":2},"chunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"passed","summary":"All assigned selectors were assessed. The current scope and chosen alternative trace the originating ISSUE’s fresh installation, ordinary supported updates, legacy and recovery jobs, direct installs, broker denial, rollback preservation and Linux compatibility. The initial predecessor/build profile, distributed trust prerequisites and guarded post-rollback routing make the supported migration boundary explicit. The cited BUILD motivates portable verification but is not presented as completed production qualification. No blocking scope defect was demonstrated.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/hldContextSlice","/body/summary","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/13","/citations/16","document:line:25","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-5d5478c61a25ac8f.json",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-3992d2e1e26124dc.json",".insrc/artifacts/BUILD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/TESTS.md","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:49","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:54","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:81","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:237","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:256","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:1-245","src/daemon/managed-release-staging.ts:99-175",".npmrc","docs/daemon.md:124-167","git:ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:package.json","git:ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/index.ts",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6.json"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Mention the initial arm64 macOS 27.0 predecessor profile in the product summary so readers can see the initial support boundary without consulting the detailed verification contract.","Label the rendered Epic and HLD metadata as framework bookkeeping; the substantive context correctly identifies the originating ISSUE and absence of a parent HLD."]},{"chunkId":"qualification","status":"changes_requested","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector and freshly assessed both prior qualification findings. The revised trust lifecycle covers admission, expiry, revocation and offline rollback. Native equivalence still lacks a transformation required by the actual independent-build evidence.","findings":[{"id":"qualification-linkedit-derived-variance","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/0/postconditions/3; LLD.md:56","message":"The permitted native transformations do not account explicitly for layout and signature-header changes caused by different debug-path lengths. The actual fs-ext study builds have __LINKEDIT filesize 11464 versus 11496, LC_SYMTAB strsize 4112 versus 4136, LC_CODE_SIGNATURE dataoff 60016 versus 60048, and CodeDirectory codeLimit 60016 versus 60048. The LLD specifies debug-root/timestamp normalization and says page hashes and LC_UUID are the only remaining variable values; validating offsets, sizes and alignment does not define how these differing values enter the compared representation. An exact comparison therefore rejects the observed legitimate variants, while silently omitting these fields would exceed the defined allowances. Specify deterministic accounting and canonicalization for the derived layout fields, string-table references and signature coverage, preserving all execution-relevant relationships. Require a positive unequal-path-length case and negative inconsistent-offset/codeLimit cases.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:54","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:56","/private/tmp/insrc-native-study-otoxp86z/first/node_modules/fs-ext/build/Release/fs_ext.node: load commands and parsed CodeDirectory","/private/tmp/insrc-native-study-otoxp86z/second-longer-path/node_modules/fs-ext/build/Release/fs_ext.node: load commands and parsed CodeDirectory","/private/tmp/insrc-native-study-otoxp86z/first.log","/private/tmp/insrc-native-study-otoxp86z/second-longer-path.log","src/daemon/managed-release-staging.ts: fingerprint and stageManagedRelease"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/9","/citations/14","/citations/15","/citations/18","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6.json","Checkpoint attempt 1: qualification-native-verifier and qualification-trust-lifecycle findings","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","src/daemon/release-compatibility.ts","src/daemon/managed-release-staging.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-preparation.ts",".npmrc","src/daemon/managed-update-handoff.ts:1-155","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts:1-245","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts:1-130","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:145-285","build-process-broker.mjs","copy-assets.mjs","package.json","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-release-staging.test.ts:1-140","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/TESTS.md","/private/tmp/insrc-native-study-otoxp86z/first.log","/private/tmp/insrc-native-study-otoxp86z/second-longer-path.log","/private/tmp/insrc-native-study-otoxp86z/first/node_modules/fs-ext/build/Release/fs_ext.node","/private/tmp/insrc-native-study-otoxp86z/second-longer-path/node_modules/fs-ext/build/Release/fs_ext.node"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Freeze concrete trust/qualification schemas, domain-tag bytes, length encoding and size limits alongside the shared signer/verifier implementation, with common signature test vectors.","Keep existing synthetic fixture passes distinct from the proposed real-product qualification matrix. No builds, tests or release activation were performed during this read-only design review."]},{"chunkId":"lifecycle","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The current contracts correct the prior rollback ordering defect by retaining the dispatcher fence through archived restoration and durable rollback publication. One remaining lifecycle gap allows the restored legacy daemon's update RPC to mutate lifecycle state before reaching that dispatcher.","findings":[{"id":"lifecycle-legacy-update-rpc-fence","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/1/postconditions; /body/errorPaths/errorCases/7; /body/testStrategy","message":"The guarded canonical dispatcher does not fence the restored predecessor's public daemon.update handler. The explicitly supported predecessor ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74 spawns its detached helper, writes daemon.update.lock and schedules its own shutdown after 250 ms without consulting InstallationMutationGate or waiting for the helper's admission. Therefore, a concurrent update RPC during archived rollback can disrupt the predecessor before terminal rollback publication even when the dispatcher rejects the eventual shell command. After rollback, the same path can stop the service before a later managed retry finishes qualification; if its reconstructed environment resolves the archive as the daemon root, it can also invoke archived mutating scripts directly. Define how this IPC route is mediated or excluded before predecessor readiness becomes public, including the rollback environment's launcher-root mapping. Add a real-predecessor RPC concurrency test before rollback publication and during a subsequent managed retry, asserting no premature shutdown, marker mutation or archived updater execution.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:80","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:194","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:260","git:ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/update-runner.ts — DAEMON_ROOT, launchUpdate and makeUpdateHandlers","git:ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts — UPDATE_SHUTDOWN_DELAY_MS and sharedAdminHandlers","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts:restoreDirectLegacyService","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-transaction.test.ts:602 — rollback fixture implements shutdown and status, without the predecessor's update RPC"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/10","/citations/11","/citations/19","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6.json — prior lifecycle assessment and current assignment","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts","src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts","src/daemon/legacy-cutover-admission.ts","src/daemon/legacy-run-guard.ts","src/daemon/legacy-drain-evidence.ts","src/daemon/fresh-managed-activation.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-launch.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-handoff.ts","src/daemon/index.ts — startup admission, managed update dispatch and shutdown lifecycle","src/daemon/update-runner.ts","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts — legacy update handler","scripts/daemon-ctl.sh — launcher roots and update routing","src/daemon/__tests__/legacy-cutover-admission.test.ts — predecessor decoding and concurrent launcher tests","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-transaction.test.ts — test inventory and legacy rollback scenarios","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-handoff.test.ts — test inventory and response-written handshake scenarios","src/daemon/__tests__/fresh-managed-activation.test.ts — test inventory","src/daemon/__tests__/legacy-run-guard.test.ts — test inventory","src/daemon/__tests__/legacy-daemon-cutover.test.ts — test inventory","git:ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/update-runner.ts","git:ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts"],"limitations":[],"advice":[]},{"chunkId":"entrypoints","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The revised design specifies independent bootstrap verification, client preflight routing, stopped-state preservation, and qualified release promotion. One managed-update ordering requirement conflicts with existing client acknowledgement deadlines.","findings":[{"id":"entrypoints-managed-preparation-ack-order","severity":"MED","location":"/body/migration/migrationSteps/5; /body/contractDetails/api/3/preconditions/0","message":"The launchManagedUpdate contract places candidate preparation before routing daemon.update to the detached helper. Preparation includes fetching, building, and inventory verification, but both IDE transports and the installed controller impose a 20-second acknowledgement deadline. A normal cold build can therefore lose its acknowledgement before the helper is launched, producing an unconfirmed update instead of the preserved launch handshake. Specify that the trusted installed helper reserves and acknowledges promptly, then performs preparation after confirmed reply delivery, with qualification still completed before shutdown or cutover. Retain the existing slow-preparation regression test in the acceptance mapping.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standal