it initial predecessor/platform profile and production qualification gate align with the ISSUE's supported-installation scope. Existing synthetic fixture results do not establish production qualification.","The sequence source agrees with the specified bootstrap, pinning, activation and archived rollback ordering, while inheriting the lifecycle and acknowledgement gaps identified by the substantive chunks.","The current companion-link finding duplicates the carried prior link defect; treat them as one defect rather than separate required corrections.","Retain the optional advice to clarify standalone bookkeeping metadata and diagram alternative branches. No additional ERD, UX mock or future workflow artifact is required by this assessment."],"findingDecisions":[{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"qualification","findingId":"qualification-native-verifier"},"rationale":"Fresh qualification inspection covers the initial toolchain, independent references, inventories and native transformations without mandatory gaps. The previous broad underspecification is narrowed to a demonstrated remaining mismatch in derived Mach-O layout and signature coverage fields.","evidenceReferences":["Checkpoint attempt 2 completedChunks: qualification, limitations=[]","LLD.md:54-56","Accepted qualification-linkedit-derived-variance: independent fs-ext builds have differing __LINKEDIT sizes, string-table sizes, signature offsets and CodeDirectory codeLimit"],"action":"superseded","reviewedInChunkIds":["qualification"],"supersededBy":{"chunkId":"qualification","findingId":"qualification-linkedit-derived-variance"}},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"qualification","findingId":"qualification-trust-lifecycle"},"rationale":"Fresh qualification inspection verifies that the revised design defines root-signed trust distribution, scoped qualification keys, freshness and replay floors, admission receipts, expiry/revocation boundaries, offline rollback and durable-success reconciliation. These address the original design omission; concrete shared encoding vectors remain optional implementation advice.","evidenceReferences":["Checkpoint attempt 2 completedChunks: qualification, limitations=[]","LLD.md:49-53","LLD.md:150","LLD.md:194-197","LLD.md:234-238","LLD.md:256-258"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["qualification"]},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"lifecycle","findingId":"lifecycle-rollback-launcher-fence"},"rationale":"Fresh lifecycle inspection verifies that canonical launcher reopening is now delayed until archived restoration and durable rollback publication. The remaining exclusivity defect is the supported predecessor's public update RPC, which can mutate state and schedule shutdown before reaching the guarded dispatcher. The fresh finding captures this residual bypass and required tests.","evidenceReferences":["Checkpoint attempt 2 completedChunks: lifecycle, limitations=[]","LLD.md:79-81","LLD.md:194-197","LLD.md:262","git:ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts: sharedAdminHandlers and UPDATE_SHUTDOWN_DELAY_MS"],"action":"superseded","reviewedInChunkIds":["lifecycle"],"supersededBy":{"chunkId":"lifecycle","findingId":"lifecycle-legacy-update-rpc-fence"}},{"source":{"attempt":1,"chunkId":"entrypoints","findingId":"entrypoints-bootstrap-before-verification"},"rationale":"Fresh entrypoint inspection verifies an explicit replacement contract: the trusted installer and IDE distributions carry an independent verifier/root and authenticate the exact bridge source before checkout, build scripts or bridge execution. Controller-boundary negative authorization tests are specified. This resolves the design omission without claiming the existing implementation already satisfies it.","evidenceReferences":["Checkpoint attempt 2 completedChunks: entrypoints, limitations=[]","LLD.md:49-50","LLD.md:234-238","LLD.md:257","Canonical /body/contractDetails/api/0/preconditions"],"action":"resolved","reviewedInChunkIds":["entrypoints"