 path mapping, job-policy preservation, durable rollback publication and guarded dispatcher settlement.","Added stageManagedInstallation and launchManagedUpdate API contracts within the existing contractDetails inventory unit.","Expanded predecessor and qualification receipt models, including archive-route identity, trust snapshot fields, authorization boundaries and offline recovery policy.","Changed rollback failure handling and added a competing-command/authorization-expiry case; expanded integration tests, fixtures and ac4 mapping.","Changed release promotion, trusted bootstrap, admission and rollback migration steps; added citations c23, c24 and c25.","Changed the sequence to include pre-execution source verification and fenced archived rollback before guarded dispatch. Participant and companion selectors remain present; the diagram document section moved from line 109 to line 158.","Scope, summary, alternatives, chosen alternative, open questions and interactionWithShared are unchanged, but their adequacy depends on the changed qualification and lifecycle contracts."],"directChunkIds":["qualification","lifecycle","entrypoints","visuals"],"indirectChunkIds":["scope"],"rationale":"Use full mode because changes span every implementation responsibility and indirectly affect the only previously passed scope chunk. The exact initial qualification profile changes the practical supported-installation boundary; trust admission affects bootstrap, candidate execution and offline recovery; archived rollback changes ownership, job reconstruction, restart/update routing, tests and sequence ordering. Unchanged requirements and alternatives therefore need renewed traceability assessment against the originating ISSUE. The preceding visuals result has a mandatory limitation and cannot be retained, and final consistency must always be fresh. No earlier coverage is reused or represented as newly reviewed. All five effective findings remain carried pending fresh inspection.","chun