, supported ordinary updates, legacy and recovery jobs, direct installs, broker denial, rollback preservation and Linux compatibility. Revised native verification, persistent rollback preload protection and acknowledgement-before-preparation remain consistent with that scope. The cited BUILD supports the need for portable verification without establishing production qualification. No blocking scope defect was demonstrated.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/hldContextSlice","/body/summary","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/13","/citations/16","document:line:25","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/restore-reliable-daemon-restart-macos-E202611103992d2e1/ISSUE.md",".insrc/artifacts/BUILD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/BUILD.md","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:49","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:54","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:57","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:80","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:125","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:188","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:455","src/daemon/managed-release-staging.ts:181","src/daemon/managed-update-preparation.ts:34","src/daemon/managed-update-preparation.ts:73","src/daemon/managed-update-launch.ts:22","src/daemon/managed-update-launch.ts:73","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts:35","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts:76","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts:193","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts:100","src/daemon/threads/admin-worker.ts",".npmrc",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6.json"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Mention the initial arm64 macOS 27.0 predecessor profile in the product summary to make the supported installation boundary immediately visible.","Label the rendered Epic and HLD metadata as framework bookkeeping so it agrees more clearly with the explicit standalone, issue-originated context."]},{"chunkId":"qualification","status":"passed","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector against the originating ISSUE, build configuration, staging and recovery code, accepted feedback, and actual unequal-path native builds. The revised representation accounts for the observed string-table, __LINKEDIT and signature-boundary variance while preserving runtime relationships and raw rollback identity. Trust admission, offline recovery, publication dependencies and planned negative coverage are consistent. No blocking design defect was demonstrated.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/9","/citations/14","/citations/15","/citations/18","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","src/daemon/release-compatibility.ts","src/daemon/managed-release-staging.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-preparation.ts",".npmrc","package.json","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh","build-process-broker.mjs","build-shutdown-watchdog.mjs","copy-assets.mjs","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts: UpdatePredecessor, journal and decoding validation","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts: release pins and rollback verification","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-release-staging.test.ts","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/TESTS.md","ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts","ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/threads/admin-worker.ts","ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/index.ts:500-590","/private/tmp/insrc-native-study-otoxp86z/first.log","/private/tmp/insrc-native-study-otoxp86z/second-longer-path.log","/private/tmp/insrc-native-study-otoxp86z/first/node_modules/fs-ext/build/Release/fs_ext.node","/private/tmp/insrc-native-study-otoxp86z/second-longer-path/node_modules/fs-ext/build/Release/fs_ext.node","Native sample inspection: original CodeDirectory page hashes verified for both files; tokenized symbol records and preserved binary prefix matched across unequal checkout-root lengths."],"limitations":[],"advice":["Freeze signer/verifier schemas, framing bytes and canonical representation rules with shared test vectors. Include legitimate suffix sharing and debug-root lengths that cross signature-page or segment-alignment boundaries.","Keep existing synthetic test results distinct from future production qualification. This review inspected existing binaries and performed in-memory comparisons; it did not execute product builds, migration tests or release activation."]},{"chunkId":"lifecycle","status":"changes_requested","summary":"All assigned selectors were inspected. The revised preload contract covers both legacy update-handler factories and worker replacements, and acknowledgement ordering aligns with the installed helper handshake. One lifecycle admission gap remains: the restored predecessor still accepts public shutdown requests outside the mutation gate.","findings":[{"id":"lifecycle-public-shutdown-admission-a3","severity":"MED","location":"/body/contractDetails/api/1/postconditions; /body/errorPaths; /body/testStrategy","message":"The rollback preload explicitly retains the original handler table except daemon.update, leaving daemon.shutdown outside InstallationMutationGate. In the pinned predecessor, that handler directly invokes shutdown in both main-thread and admin-worker routing; an existing JetBrains Stop action calls this RPC directly, bypassing the canonical dispatcher. Consequently, a concurrent shutdown can stop the restored predecessor while rollback settlement still owns the reservation, or during preparation for a later managed retry. This defeats the stated lifecycle fence and can invalidate the running state verified for rollback publication. Specify admission for public shutdown while a reservation is active, distinguishing the authorized migration controller's drain from competing clients. Extend the real-predecessor tests to send shutdown before rollback publication and during later preparation, including threaded routing and worker replacement.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:80-84 — fenced restoration and original-table preservation except daemon.update","git:ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts:93-97 — daemon.shutdown invokes the supplied shutdown callback","git:ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/threads/admin-worker.ts:40-41 — worker shutdown forwards to the main-thread shutdown service","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/daemon/DaemonGateway.kt:1373 — shutdown calls METHOD_SHUTDOWN directly","src/daemon/managed-daemon-lifecycle.ts:publicShutdown — managed public shutdown requires parent admission before local drain","/body/testStrategy/testLevels/7 — proposed restored-predecessor concurrency coverage exercises daemon.update but does not specify shutdown admission"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/contractDetails","/body/dataModelChanges","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/1","/citations/2","/citations/3","/citations/4","/citations/5","/citations/6","/citations/10","/citations/11","/citations/19","/citations/20","/citations/21","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6.json — prior lifecycle finding and current qualification feedback","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","src/shared/managed-daemon-installation.ts","src/shared/installation-mutation-gate.ts","src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-recovery.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-preparation.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-launch.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-handoff.ts","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts","src/bin/insrc-daemon-update.ts","src/daemon/legacy-launch-job.ts","src/daemon/legacy-daemon-cutover.ts","src/daemon/legacy-cutover-admission.ts","src/daemon/legacy-run-guard.ts","src/daemon/fresh-managed-activation.ts","src/daemon/index.ts — startup, routing, worker creation and shutdown","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts","src/daemon/threads/admin-worker.ts","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts","src/daemon/threads/supervisor.ts","src/daemon/managed-daemon-lifecycle.ts","src/cli/services/daemon.ts — direct legacy shutdown and managed stop routing","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/daemon/DaemonGateway.kt — direct shutdown IPC","src/daemon/__tests__/legacy-cutover-admission.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/legacy-daemon-cutover.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/legacy-run-guard.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-transaction.test.ts — publication recovery and legacy rollback fixtures","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-handoff.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/fresh-managed-activation.test.ts — activation intent and interruption coverage","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-ipc.test.ts — test inventory","git:ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts","git:ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/update-runner.ts","git:ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/handler-runtime.ts — sharedAdminHandlers import and table construction","git:ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/index.ts — lazy main handler construction and queued admin routing","git:ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/threads/admin-worker.ts","git:ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/threads/workers.ts — default execArgv inheritance","git:ab6a96296ea6f2bde948636424218c0a23136c74:src/daemon/threads/supervisor.ts — replacement uses the same worker creation path","https://nodejs.org/download/release/v22.23.2/docs/api/module.html","https://nodejs.org/download/release/v22.23.2/docs/api/cli.html"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Make the preload receipt format explicit: bind the restoration generation, process incarnation, worker identity, configuration digest and preload digest, and reject stale receipts.","The pinned Node runtime supports synchronous hooks and preload inheritance through default worker execArgv. Preserve these assumptions in profile qualification tests. See [Node module hooks](https://nodejs.org/download/release/v22.23.2/docs/api/module.html#synchronous-hooks-accepted-by-moduleregisterhooks).","Runtime migration and launchd tests were not executed during this read-only design assessment. Existing synthetic rollback fixtures do not establish the proposed real-predecessor preload behavior."]},{"chunkId":"entrypoints","status":"passed","summary":"Inspected every assigned selector and the relevant installer, shell, TUI, admin, detached updater, VS Code and JetBrains paths. The revised acknowledgement contract preserves client deadlines, confirms response writing before preparation, cancels unstarted work after failed delivery, survives subsequent disconnects, and correlates terminal outcomes. Installer routing, bootstrap authentication, stopped-state intent, Linux preservation and release promotion requirements align with the originating issue. No blocking design defects were demonstrated in this assignment.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/summary","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/0","/citations/7","/citations/8","/citations/12","/citations/17","/citations/22","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-5d5478c61a25ac8f.json","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh:164-223,457-475","scripts/daemon-ctl.sh:258-400","src/cli/services/maintenance.ts:108-125","src/bin/insrc-daemon-control.ts:managed update routing","src/bin/insrc-daemon-update.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-preparation.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-launch.ts","src/daemon/update-runner.ts:launchUpdate","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts:sharedAdminHandlers and adminWorkerHandlers","src/daemon/threads/admin-worker.ts:admin handler construction","src/daemon/index.ts:535-543","src/daemon/server.ts:189-211,393-430","src/daemon/managed-update-ipc.ts","src/shared/ipc-client.ts:244","src/shared/update-source.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-handoff.test.ts:127-243","src/daemon/__tests__/fixtures/managed-update-launch-child.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/macos-upgrade-routing.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-release-staging.test.ts:qualification and broker-denial fixtures","src/daemon/__tests__/fresh-managed-activation.test.ts:installer fixtures","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-ipc.test.ts:test coverage","src/daemon/__tests__/linux-installed-lifecycle.test.ts","src/daemon/__tests__/fixtures/linux-installed-lifecycle.sh","vscode-plugin/src/daemon/controller.ts","vscode-plugin/src/daemon/paths.ts","vscode-plugin/src/freshness/daemon-freshness.ts:202-298","vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts:225-244","vscode-plugin/package.json:917-921","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/lifecycle/ScriptDaemonProvisioner.kt","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/lifecycle/DaemonLifecycleCommandRunner.kt","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/lifecycle/DaemonLifecycleService.kt:DefaultDaemonScriptLocator","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/freshness/DaemonFreshnessFlow.kt:116-202","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/freshness/InstalledCommitFreshnessConsumer.kt:production wiring","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/daemon/UnixSocketDaemonRpc.kt:bounded update replies","jetbrains-plugin/build.gradle.kts:installer resource packaging","docs/daemon.md:macOS installed lifecycle and configured update source"],"limitations":[],"advice":["The current routing fixture expects clone/build/controller execution before authorization. Update that expectation when implementing the proposed trusted bootstrap; its current success cannot establish the revised security contract.","Existing installer and broker-denial fixtures use synthetic product programs. Preserve the LLD's separate requirement for independent production builds and immutable real-product qualification receipts before promotion.","No installation, launchd or release qualification tests were executed during this read-only design review."]},{"chunkId":"visuals","status":"incomplete","summary":"Inspected the complete sequence definition, all participants, companion source and live link against the issue and current contracts. The sequence misrepresents mutually exclusive lifecycle paths, and the companion link remains broken. Actual rendering verification remains technically unavailable.","findings":[{"id":"visuals-a3-unconditional-lifecycle","severity":"MED","location":"/body/sequenceDefinition/messages/8","message":"The generated sequence presents Start child → Verify readiness → Verify idle → Commit success → Reconcile candidate → Restore archived prior → Publish rollback as one unconditional call order. This contradicts the running/idle alternatives and the rule that durable success must never roll back. The description table qualifies some messages, but those conditions are absent from the diagram itself. Represent running versus idle and success versus uncommitted failure as explicit alternatives, retaining the stopped predecessor condition on restoration.","evidenceReferences":[".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json: /body/sequenceDefinition/messages/8 through /14","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html: embedded Mermaid source and Messages table","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md: sections 2.2, 2.3 and migration steps 6–7","src/daemon/managed-update-handoff.ts: stageManagedCandidate returns without starting a child for a stopped predecessor","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts: settleManagedUpdate and recoverManagedTransaction separate committed activation from rollback"]},{"id":"visuals-a3-relative-companion-link","severity":"LOW","location":"docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:163","message":"The live document still links to docs/standalone/.../S001/sequence-diagram.html from inside that same directory. Standard Markdown resolution produces a nonexistent nested path. The companion exists at the repository-relative path recorded in companions; the document link should resolve relative to LLD.md. Fresh inspection confirms the same underlying defect reported by both earlier companion-link findings.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md:163",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json: /body/companions/0/relPath","Filesystem resolution: document-relative link target absent; repository-relative companion present",".insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6.json: attempt 1 visuals-relative-companion-link and attempt 2 visuals-current-relative-link"]}],"inspectedReferences":["/body/sequenceDefinition","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/0","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/1","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/2","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/3","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/4","/body/sequenceDefinition/participants/5","/body/companions","document:line:161","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html","src/daemon/managed-update-handoff.ts","src/daemon/managed-update-transaction.ts"],"limitations":["Mandatory actual rendering inspection of docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html was retried through the browser tool, which returned 'The browser access host is unavailable'. HTML, embedded Mermaid and description tables were inspected, but rendered legibility, clipping and layout could not be verified."],"advice":["The sequence correctly describes bootstrap authentication before checkout, qualification and raw pinning before fencing, and preload-protected archived rollback. Consider adding the separately contracted managed acknowledgement-before-preparation path and provisional selector publication to make those ordering boundaries visible.","The ownership and relationship prose is sufficient for this assignment; no additional ERD or UX mock is necessary solely because of artifact size."]},{"chunkId":"consistency","status":"incomplete","summary":"Reconciled all five fresh substantive assessments against the originating ISSUE and current canonical/live LLD. All 47 inventory selectors have declared inspection coverage, and current fingerprints match the reviewed baseline. Three prior findings are resolved; both prior companion-link origins remain carried. Accepted fresh feedback identifies two MED defects. Mandatory rendered-diagram verification remains incomplete.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/tmp/design-review/macos-portable-qualification-5d5478c6.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/sequence-diagram.html","Checkpoint attempts 1 and 2: accepted completed feedback, preceding report and effectiveFindingOrigins","Checkpoint attempt 3 completedChunks: scope, qualification, lifecycle, entrypoints and visuals","Checkpoint attempt 3 pl