ed section and cited lifecycle source, including completeLegacyMigration, activation reservations, predecessor variants, historical decoding and shared installation contracts.","Verify state-root ownership and cardinality, canonical checkout exchange, exclusion of old mutators, process and socket authentication, exact exit observation, drain classification and uninterrupted run-file guard transfer.","Trace fresh running and idle activation, managed running and stopped updates, legacy job/direct/stopped migration, partial publication cleanup, rollback launch reconstruction and durable outcome recovery.","Assess errors and tests alongside each transition, including broker-denied or unknown drain, candidate bootstrap failure, interruption, lost publication acknowledgement and fenced uncertainty."],"dependsOn":["qualification"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"entrypoints","title":"Installer and client integration, rollout and acceptance coverage","selectors":["/body/summary","/body/interactionWithShared","/body/errorPaths","/body/testStrategy","/body/migration","/citations/0","/citations/7","/citations/8","/citations/12"],"concerns":["Inspect every assigned section and cited installer, shell, update runner and admin-handler source; follow necessary current CLI, VS Code and JetBrains call sites.","Check that supported ordinary installation and update actions reach preflight before shutdown, including updated freshness clients and the stated limitation of already-installed older binaries.","Verify configured source, branch, root, CLI flags and IPC result compatibility, explicit start intent, Linux preservation and practical release-to-migration dependency order.","Check acceptance mapping against the originating ISSUE and actual named scenarios, fixtures and release promotion obligations; assess whether user-facing outcomes distinguish verified success, rollback and uncertainty."],"dependsOn":["lifecycle"],"purpose":"substantive"},{"id":"visuals","title":"Sequence definit