,"chunkIds":["lifecycle"]},{"unitId":"/citations/12","chunkIds":["entrypoints"]},{"unitId":"/citations/13","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/14","chunkIds":["qualification"]},{"unitId":"/citations/15","chunkIds":["qualification"]},{"unitId":"/citations/16","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"/citations/17","chunkIds":["entrypoints"]},{"unitId":"/citations/18","chunkIds":["qualification"]},{"unitId":"/citations/19","chunkIds":["lifecycle"]},{"unitId":"/citations/20","chunkIds":["lifecycle"]},{"unitId":"/citations/21","chunkIds":["lifecycle"]},{"unitId":"/citations/22","chunkIds":["entrypoints"]},{"unitId":"document:line:25","chunkIds":["scope"]},{"unitId":"document:line:161","chunkIds":["visuals"]}]},"impact":{"baselineAttempt":2,"mode":"full","changes":["stageManagedRelease now specifies checked physical Mach-O layouts, tokenized string-table reconstruction, derived canonical extents, signature-boundary/codeLimit accounting and preservation of runtime relationships.","completeLegacyMigration now requires a trusted pinned Node preload wrapping both legacy admin handler factories, main/admin-worker coverage including replacements, startup receipts, persistent old-update refusal and a distinct guarded launcher root.","UpdatePredecessor now binds the rollback preload and supported import/worker topology to the archive route and restoration generation.","launchManagedUpdate now reserves and acknowledges using the trusted installed helper before preparation, waits for confirmed reply delivery and cancels only unstarted work after delivery failure.","Error handling adds failed preload binding and restored legacy update requests. Tests and acceptance mapping add unequal-length native-build cases, malformed layout/signature cases, real old IPC containment and acknowledgement timing/delivery cases.","Migration steps incorporate acknowledgement-before-preparation and preload-protected restoration. The sequence's archived-restoration description also adds old-update blocking.","Three citations were added for admin-handlers.ts, threads/admin-worker.ts and managed-update-handoff.test.ts. The diagram section moved from line 158 to line 161; companion metadata retains the same path.","The product summary, standalone context, alternatives and originating ISSUE remain substantively unchanged, but their feasibility and scope claims depend on the revised qualification and rollback mechanisms."],"directChunkIds":["qualification","lifecycle","entrypoints","visuals"],"indirectChunkIds":["scope"],"rationale":"Attempt 2 is the immediately preceding completed assessment. Its accepted plan, chunk feedback, report, finding decisions and captured canonical/live baseline were compared with the current documents and inventory. Full review is selected because the revisions directly affect qualification, lifecycle, entrypoint contracts and the linked sequence, while indirectly affecting unchanged supported-scope claims. The native representation changes what installations can qualify; the preload changes executable ownership, restoration admission and later update routing; acknowledgement ordering changes reservation timing and failure recovery. These effects cross shared contract, error, test and migration sections. Scope therefore also requires fresh inspection rather than retaining its prior pass. Attempt 2 visuals and final consistency were incomplete, so neither can be retained or replaced by older coverage. No coverage is retained. All five effective finding origins are carried exactly as recorded by attempt 2, including both link-defect origins; no finding is resolved during impact preparation.","uncertainReason":"Selective retention is not justified: changes propagate across all implementation responsibilities and the unchanged scope depends on their feasibility. Prior mandatory rendered-diagram verification also remains incomplete and requires a fresh attempt.","chunkMapping":[{"priorIds":["scope"],"currentIds":["scope"],"explanation":"Same se