ension explicit during implementation: existing recoverStoppedLifecycle requires quiescence, while a controller can die before the admitted legacy drain begins or before stale run files are reconciled. Exercise both boundaries with the proposed real-predecessor owner-death tests.","Treat the real predecessor, worker replacement and JetBrains-compatible shutdown cases as new verification work; the inspected existing cutover fixture uses a synthetic socket server and does not establish adapter containment."]},{"chunkId":"entrypoints","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The assigned sections cover installer/client routing, acknowledgement delivery, rollback containment, release promotion and Linux preservation. One ordering inconsistency leaves public shutdown admission during a restored legacy update’s preparation undefined.","findings":[{"id":"entrypoints-restored-preparation-admission-a4","severity":"MED","location":"/body/migration/migrationSteps/2–3 and /body/migration/migrationSteps/6","message":"Specify preparation admission for a later update of the restored legacy daemon. Steps 3–4 stage and verify the candidate before reserving legacy cutover, while step 7 requires public shutdown during preparation to return busy. The adapter rejects shutdown only when another reservation exists; without early admission, it can accept a stop during fetch/build/inventory. The current prepareLegacyUpgrade follows precisely this stage-before-reserve ordering. Define when the guarded external update acquires its preparation reservation, how it captures running/stopped intent, and how verification failure releases it. Add a paused-preparation test through the actual restored installer route so the promised busy behavior is enforced before cutover.","evidenceReferences":["docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md: Migration steps 3, 4 and 7","LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json /body/errorPaths/edgeCases/2: stage candidate before acqu