ation 23","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/23","selector":"/citations/23","title":"Citation 24","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/24","selector":"/citations/24","title":"Citation 25","kind":"citation"},{"id":"/citations/25","selector":"/citations/25","title":"Citation 26","kind":"citation"},{"id":"document:line:25","selector":"document:line:25","title":"1. HLD context","kind":"section"},{"id":"document:line:164","selector":"document:line:164","title":"4. Diagrams","kind":"section"}]},"completedChunks":[{"chunkId":"scope","status":"passed","summary":"All assigned scope selectors were assessed. The design traces the originating ISSUE across fresh installation, supported updates, legacy and recovery jobs, direct installs, broker denial, data preservation and running/stopped rollback. The restored-process adapter, public stop admission and private controller drain preserve that intent. Production qualification remains an explicit release prerequisite; the cited BUILD is supporting evidence rather than proof of completed qualification. No blocking scope defect was demonstrated.","findings":[],"inspectedReferences":["/body/hldContextSlice","/body/summary","/body/alternativesConsidered","/body/alternativesConsidered/0","/body/alternativesConsidered/1","/body/alternativesConsidered/2","/body/chosenAlternative","/body/openQuestions","/citations/13","/citations/16","document:line:25","/Users/subhagho/work/projects/insors/insrc/docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/LLD.md",".insrc/artifacts/LLD-5d5478c61a25ac8f-s1.json",".insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-5d5478c61a25ac8f.json","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/ISSUE.md","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/BUILD.md","docs/standalone/enable-managed-daemon-lifecycle-macos-install-E202611115d5478c6/S001/TESTS.md:200","scripts/insrc-daemon-install.sh",".npmrc","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts:97",