r","src/daemon/admin-handlers.ts — public shutdown and delayed update shutdown","src/daemon/index.ts — startup guard, main routing and shutdown callbacks","src/daemon/threads/admin-worker.ts","src/daemon/threads/main-services.ts — worker shutdown service","src/daemon/threads/workers.ts — worker construction and inherited startup arguments","src/daemon/threads/supervisor.ts — worker replacement and queued routing","src/daemon/supervisor.ts — public stop ownership and exact child reconciliation","src/cli/services/managed-daemon-control.ts — stop reservation and abandoned lifecycle recovery","jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/daemon/DaemonGateway.kt:1373 — direct shutdown RPC and framed-error handling","src/daemon/__tests__/legacy-daemon-cutover.test.ts — existing synthetic exact-exit coverage","src/daemon/__tests__/managed-update-handoff.test.ts — existing handoff and acknowledgement fixtures"],"limitations":[],"advice":["Make the restored-legacy stop recovery extension explicit during implementation: existing recoverStoppedLifecycle requires quiescence, while a controller can die before the admitted legacy drain begins or before stale run files are reconciled. Exercise both boundaries with the proposed real-predecessor owner-death tests.","Treat the real predecessor, worker replacement and JetBrains-compatible shutdown cases as new verification work; the inspected existing cutover fixture uses a synthetic socket server and does not establish adapter containment."]},{"chunkId":"entrypoints","status":"changes_requested","summary":"The assigned sections cover installer/client routing, acknowledgement delivery, rollback containment, release promotion and Linux preservation. One ordering inconsistency leaves public shutdown admission during a restored legacy update’s preparation undefined.","findings":[{"id":"entrypoints-restored-preparation-admission-a4","severity":"MED","location":"/body/migration/migrationSteps/2–3 and /body/migration/migration